================================================================================
PROJECT PURPOSE & OFFICIAL DISTRIBUTION NOTICE
================================================================================

This software, "AD Remote Control Center Enterprise", was originally created by
Askarali Mattummal for personal use in Windows Active Directory enterprise
administration. Following requests from colleagues and fellow IT professionals,
it has been released publicly to assist IT administrators, systems engineers, and
helpdesk specialists with daily domain management tasks.

The software was specifically developed to be:
  * Safe to use and non-intrusive
  * Fully portable — requires no installer, agents, or third-party dependencies
  * Lightweight, responsive, and resource-efficient for IT administrators
  * Comprehensive — unifying Active Directory user management, workstation remote
    control (Remote Shadow & RDP), printer queue control, network shares, live
    telemetry, and diagnostic functions into a single administrative console.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OFFICIAL RELEASE SOURCE & INTEGRITY VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The ONLY official, authentic, and verified source for downloading this
software and its updates is the official GitHub repository:

  👉 https://github.com/SuperUser-exe/AD-Remote-Control-Center

IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTICE:
  1. Unofficial Sources: If you obtain this application from any third-party
     website, file-sharing platform, mirror, or unauthorized repository, the
     author (Askarali Mattummal) assumes NO responsibility or liability for any
     malfunction, security issue, data loss, or damages resulting from the use
     of that unofficial or modified copy.
  2. Integrity: Users must always download releases directly from the official
     GitHub repository and verify the release SHA-256 checksums provided in
     CHECKSUMS.txt.
  3. Binary Protection: Production public releases of this software are protected
     using multi-layered code obfuscation and string encryption to preserve
     project integrity and prevent unauthorized malicious tampering or repackaging.
     For detailed information regarding our binary protection architecture,
     please consult:
       docs/PUBLIC_RELEASE_AND_PROTECTION_PLAN.md

